{
 "result": "fibmod.py is the adopted bin()-string fast-doubling variant. It reads all stdin tokens, reduces each n mod the Pisano period 2(M+1), and computes fib(n) mod 1e9+7 with the doubling identities, one loop over the binary digits of n. It passed the sample checks (fib(10)=55 and in-0/out-0 matched) and the assay registered a baseline of 4.30053 with 3.4% noise. The last variant was adopted at +9%. I'm stopping here since further gains would need to beat noise by more than 3.4% and the remaining ideas are small.",
